# MongoDB backup

Owner rules live in the Service, not in this rule.

- [mongodb-backup](../../docs/knowledge/services/mongodb-backup.md)
- [operator playbook](../../docs/mongodb-backup-automation/README.md)
- [catalog](../../docs/index.md)

Software-only notes:

- Job package is `scripts/cloud/mongodb-backup/` (committed). Do not put it under `scripts/dev_ops/`.
- Runtime is the Cloud Run Job in GCP project `vantage-sheets-496816`. Archives are `gs://vantage-mongodb-backups-496816`. Not AWS S3, not `gs://vantage-sheets-496816/`.
- Never print, commit, or log `MONGO_URI`. Secret name only: `vantage-production-mongo-uri`.
- Tests are `npm test` in the job package. They must not contact MongoDB or GCS.
- Restore drills remap into an isolated database. Never `--drop` against `vantagemovers`.
